your run of 12 October used `reg` with `weights:`, affected by issue 123, fixed in 0.9.2
  scripts/main.zeff on Zeff 0.9.0: `reg` with `weights:` gave standard errors that left the weights out of the residual variance
  an analysis is affected when the weights were not all equal

Zeff 0.9.0, which this project pins, has 3 known wrong results: issue 123 (`reg` with `weights:`, `ivreg` with `weights:`), fixed in 0.9.2; issue 131 (`confusion`), fixed in 0.9.1; issue 140 (`margins` with `at:` or `type:`), not yet corrected
  the pin does not move by itself: `zeff engine use 0.9.2` runs the project on both engines, says what differs, and moves it
1 run read against the 4 issues known to Zeff 0.9.3
